  "notes": "The cathedral vicar’s architectural history records the triple arched porch supported by paired columns, façade mosaic, grand rose window, twin square towers with tiara-like cupolas and Lorraine crosses, crossing dome and rounded apse. The Church inventory describes pale stone from Djebel-Oust and the 1910 tower completion."
